## How the Task List works
// The Task List example is a to-do list:  type a task, tick it off when it's done,
// and choose whether to see them all, only the ones to do, or only the ones done.
// Three ideas do the work:
// - each task is a THING of its own, which draws itself as a row with a checkbox
// - the list picks tasks out with "where":  "tasks in its tasks where it is active"
// - the list draws each task, or skips it, as its filter says
//
// This guide keeps those three, and leaves out dragging, selecting, the property editor,
// and where the tasks are kept:  here they're in memory, and start afresh each run.
// Open Task List, in the Examples, for all of it.  Lista de tareas is the same list, written in Spanish.


## A task
a "task" is a view where:
	- its "title" is text
	- its "done" is yes or no
	- it "is done" if its done is yes
	- it "is active" if its done is no

	// a form of its own, bound to the task:  ticking the box changes its "done"
	- to draw it:
		return <ui-form value={it}>
			<ui-stack direction="horizontal" spacing="sm">
				<ui-checkbox name="done" aria-label="Done"/>
				<ui-text>{its title}</ui-text>
			</ui-stack>
		</ui-form>


## The checklist:  the tasks, shown as its filter says
a "checklist" is a viewable list of tasks where:
	// what it shows:  every task, the ones still to do, or the ones done
	- its "showing" is one of all, active or done
	// each task in turn, unless the filter hides it:  "return nothing" draws nothing
	- to draw each item:
		if its showing is "active" and the task is done return nothing
		if its showing is "done" and the task is active return nothing
		return draw the task

a task belongs to one checklist


## The app
task list is an app where:
	- its "tasks" is a new checklist
	// how many are left:  the tasks picked out with "where", counted
	- its "active count" is the length of (tasks in its tasks where it is active)

	- to draw it:
		return <ui-container text>
			<ui-menu appearance="secondary">
				<ui-item kind="header">{its active count + " to do"}</ui-item>
				<ui-item selected={the showing of its tasks is "all"} onClick={set the showing of its tasks to "all"}>All</ui-item>
				<ui-item selected={the showing of its tasks is "active"} onClick={set the showing of its tasks to "active"}>To do</ui-item>
				<ui-item selected={the showing of its tasks is "done"} onClick={set the showing of its tasks to "done"}>Done</ui-item>
			</ui-menu>
			{draw its tasks}
		</ui-container>


## Start:  three tasks, one of them done
set the showing of the tasks of the task list to all
add (a new task with title = "Read this guide", done = yes) to the tasks of the task list
add (a new task with title = "Tick a box on the right") to the tasks of the task list
add (a new task with title = "Try the To do filter") to the tasks of the task list


## A check
to test counting the tasks to do
	set the list to a new checklist
	add (a new task with title = "a", done = yes) to the list
	add (a new task with title = "b") to the list
	the length of (tasks in the list where it is active) should be 1


